invariant: INV-43
file: p256_wide_verify_point.c
catches: p256_verify_equiv_test
reason: the host verifier's pass over the two scalars' digits reads no
  digit of u1, so it adds no multiple of G, R is u2*Q and the verifier
  accepts only a signature whose hash is zero modulo n.
  bin/p256_verify_equiv_test requires the 32-bit verifier's verdict on
  every signature it tries.

--- old
    int g_len = signed_digits(g_digits, u1);
--- new
    (void)u1;
    memset(g_digits, 0, sizeof g_digits);
    int g_len = 0;
